  "notes": "Drawn from three dated photos of N582UW (2024-02-15, 2025-11-18), all of the left side. The fin title shows only as 'PS' before the tailplane; 'PSA' is from the scheme's description. The belly is plain silver in the departing shots; the right side not seen. Re-checked 2026-11-15: the cheatlines' wrap round the nose, the smile and the fin's sweeping bands drawn as curves (straight runs kept straight by corners at their aft ends); 'American' (x 0.20-0.285) agrees with the doors on the 2024-02-15 photo; 'PSA' on the fin is given a length of 0.35 of the chord, an estimate, since the tailplane hides its end in every photo. No measured A321 shape yet.",
  "history": "Previously on A319 N742PS."
